The  and  commands  reference  NIS  (YP) maps as specified by the
user.  Occasionally it is desirable to use a shorthand  reference
for  a longer map name, hence the file, kept in The format of the
file is one pair per line.  The default installed nickname map is
as follows: passwd.byname group.byname networks.byaddr  hosts.by‐
name protocols.bynumber services.byname aliases.byname ethers.by‐
name  master.passwd.byname A blank or incomplete file will affect
any scripts which use nicknames for map lookup,  whereas  if  the
file  is  simply  missing,  the  default compiled‐in list will be
used.  The file first appeared in Solaris 2.4.
